# JSON edge cases: PowerShell 5.1's exact writer and lenient reader (D29)
odd has
    tricky is "a,b:{c}[d]\"e\" \ end"
.
convert odd to json into text
say text
rows are
    1
    2
.
grid are
    "x"
.
remove "x" from grid
add rows to grid
add rows to grid
convert grid to json into gridText
say gridText
holder has
    rows is grid
    stamp is date from "2000-02-29 13:45:10"
.
convert holder to json into holderText
say holderText
pointThree is 0.1 plus 0.2
convert pointThree to json into sum
say sum
convert 123456789012345678 to json into big
say big
oneEighth is 1 divided by 8
convert oneEighth to json into eighth
say eighth
convert true to json into yes
say yes
convert "" to json into blank
say blank
inputs are
    "01"
    "+1"
    "1."
    ".5"
    "1-"
    "-0"
    "1e2"
    "1E-2"
    "2147483648"
    "9223372036854775808"
    "123456789012345678901234567890"
    "0.1"
    "3.14159265358979323846"
    "NaN"
    "Infinity"
    "-Infinity"
    "'single'"
    "\"\u00e9\t|\""
    "{a:1,b_c:2}"
    "{\"x\":1,\"x\":2,\"y\":3}"
    "[1,[2,[3,[]]],{}]"
    "{}"
    "[]"
    "  true  "
    "null"
    "1e400"
    "1_000"
    "0x10"
    "TRUE"
    "[1,2,]"
    "{\"a\":1,}"
    "[1 2]"
    "\"\x\""
    "{\"\":1}"
    "{\"a\":1,\"A\":2}"
    "\"unterminated"
    "[] extra"
    "\"\u12\""
.
for each source in inputs
    try
        convert source from json into value
        say source "=>" value
    otherwise into reason
        say source "=>" reason
    .
.
convert "{\"x\":1,\"x\":2,\"y\":3}" from json into dup
convert dup to json into dupText
say dupText
